  "question": {
    "text": "Solid $\\mathrm{Ba}\\left(\\mathrm{NO}_3\\right)_2$ is gradually dissolved in a $1.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~M} \\mathrm{~Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$ solution. At which concentration of $\\mathrm{Ba}^{2+}$, precipitate of $\\mathrm{BaCO}_3$ begins to form ? $\\left(K_{s p}\\right.$ for $\\left.\\mathrm{BaCO}_3=5.1 \\times 10^{-9}\\right)$",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "V6lyK",
      "text": "\n$5.1 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "4xdHg",
      "text": "\n$7.1 \\times 10^{-8} \\mathrm{M}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "yKZxc",
      "text": "\n$4.1 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "6mLVi",
      "text": "\n$8.1 \\times 10^{-7} \\mathrm{M}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given $\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3=1.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\therefore \\quad\\left[\\mathrm{CO}_3^{--}\\right]=1.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M} \\\\\n& \\text { i.e. } \\quad \\mathrm{s}=1.0 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{M}\n\\end{aligned}$\nAt equilibrium\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& {\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{++}\\right]\\left[\\mathrm{CO}_3{ }^{--}\\right]=\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}} \\text { of } \\mathrm{BaCO}_3} \\\\\n& {\\left[\\mathrm{Ba}^{++}\\right]=\\frac{\\mathrm{K}_{\\mathrm{sp}}}{\\left[\\mathrm{CO}_3{ }^{--}\\right]}=\\frac{5.1 \\times 10^{-9}}{1.0 \\times 10^{-4}}}\n\\end{aligned}$\n$=5.1 \\times 10^{-5} \\mathrm{M}$",
    "image": null
  },
